    "explanation": "The cerebellar white matter contains a complex network of afferent and efferent fibers, including climbing and mossy fibers, which transmit signals from various sources to the cerebellar cortex. The efferent fibers, originating from Purkinje cells, project to the deep nuclei or vestibular nuclei, enabling the cerebellum to regulate motor functions such as balance, posture, and coordination. The internal core of folia in the cerebellum is formed by these white matter tracts, which are essential for the cerebellum's role in motor learning and adaptation.",
