    "text": "What is special about Purkinje cell output?",
    "modelAnswer": "Purkinje cells are the only output of cerebellar cortex\nThey are inhibitory\nProject mainly to deep cerebellar nuclei\nSome project directly to vestibular nuclei (flocculonodular lobe)",
    "keyConcept": "Purkinje cells are the primary output neurons of the cerebellar cortex.",
    "explanation": "Purkinje cells are unique in that they are the only output neurons of the cerebellar cortex, serving as the final common pathway for cerebellar processing. As inhibitory interneurons, they play a crucial role in regulating the activity of downstream neurons, primarily projecting to the deep cerebellar nuclei and, in some cases, directly to the vestibular nuclei in the flocculonodular lobe. This distinctive output mechanism allows the cerebellum to modulate motor coordination and learning through precise control over neural activity.",
    "tags": []
