    "explanation": "The spinal nucleus and tract of the trigeminal nerve play a crucial role in the transmission of pain and temperature sensations from the face to the brain. This is achieved through the descending afferents of the trigeminal nerve, which synapse in the spinal trigeminal nucleus and then send secondary fibers to cross and ascend as the trigeminothalamic tract. Ultimately, these fibers terminate in the ventral posteromedial (VPM) nucleus of the thalamus, where they are further processed and relayed to the cortex for perception.",
